'''Bandits''' are enemies that inhabit the [[Bandit Camp (Wilderness)]]. The bandits are guarded by [[Guard Bandit]]s. These bandits are [[Aggressiveness|aggressive]], so players should take caution when approaching the camp. The camp's champions, however, such as [[Donny the lad]], are not aggressive.

==Strategy==
Players who receive Bandits as a [[Slayer task]] may trap 5 of the level 130 Bandits in the Pizza shop house and the General Store house. One of the level 130 Bandits in the northern area of the Bandit Camp cannot be trapped, as his [[aggro]] range does not extend to the houses - he will de-aggro players who try to trap him in the huts. But players may freely kill the Level 22 and 34 Bandits without expensive protective gear or Prayer-boosting armour, if they trap the five level 130s that they can, and as long as they keep an eye out for the single level 130.

If killing the single Bandit in the Wilderness Slayer Cave, he will respawn almost instantly, as opposed to the 60s it may normally take.

If using a halberd you can safe spot bandits by standing on the north side of the table at fat Tony's.

If you'd like to prioritize barraging the level 130 bandits, you can setup a cannon slightly southwest of the first spear wall near the entrance. This extends the task as you'll only rarely target a single lower level bandit. When you take in consideration their far aggressive range, high hitpoints and fast respawn time make it an effective task for experience.

